\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I love to think, though I am young,
\par My Saviour was a child;
\par That Jesus walked this earth along,
\par With feet all undefiled.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He kept His Father's word of truth,
\par As I am taught to do;
\par And while He walked the paths of youth
\par He walked in wisdom too.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I love to think that He who spake
\par And made the blind to see,
\par And called the sleeping death to wake,
\par Was once a child like me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. That He who wore the thorny crown,
\par And tasted death's despair,
\par Had a kind mother like my own,
\par And knew her love and care.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. I know 'twas all for love of me
\par That He became a child,
\par And left the heavens, so fair to see,
\par And trod earth's pathway wild.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Then, Saviour, who wast once a child,
\par A child may come to Thee;
\par And O in all the mercy mild,
\par Dear Saviour, come to me!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

